*** Settings ***
Documentation     [SUITE PURPOSE]  Verification of 5GC001857-A
...               Scope : Test new PRACH configuration index introduced by 1857 (=spillover 580-D)
...                       The scenario is to configure the gNB with usable frame structure
...                       for the PRACH CI and perform UE attach
...                       08-10-2021              |           1857 refactoring
...                       14-Sept-2021            |           Updates for mmW (same strategy as for 1347)

Resource          resources/robot/5GC001857-A_Keywords.robot


*** Variables ***


*** Keywords ***
TC_1857_PRACH_CI
    [Documentation]                 Generic test for all PRACH CI introduced by 1857 (FR1 and FR2)
    [Arguments]                     ${band}
    ...                             ${prach_ci_value}
    ...                             ${tl_topology}=classical

    Set Suitable PRACH              band=${band}         prach_ci_value=${prach_ci_value}       tl_type=${tl_topology}    

	#In case of mmW set the ueid to 1, for NSA call
	Run Keyword If                  "${band}"=="mmW"	Run Keywords
	...								Run    sed -i 's/set_ue simulated id=11 /set_ue simulated id=1 /g' ${tl.core.dir_path}/${tl.core.cfg_filename}
	...								AND 
	...								Run    sed -i 's/ue_param id=11 /ue_param id=1 /g' ${tl.core.dir_path}/${tl.core.cfg_filename}
	     
    
	WTS Setup

    # Cellsetup is now done, Sherpa can be enabled if needed
    Run Keyword If                  ${enable_sherpa} == ${True}           Activate Sherpa
    

	
    # Capture X2 to check PRACH configuration sent to UE
    # UE attach to 4G+5G (NSA)
    ${CaptureCPRT_X2} =              SgNB Addition to ENB                 ueSetting=${UE_SIMPLE}
    ...                                                                   withTN=True

    # If attach was successful, it's enough as PRACH CI configured inside SCF was used.
    # Anyway, check PRACH CI sent to UE to be sure the right CI was used.
    Check PrachConfigIndex in RRC Reconfiguration           ${CaptureCPRT_X2}       ${prach_ci_value}

    # Detach UE
    UE Detach Enb                   ueSetting=${UE_SIMPLE}
